⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
301 calories 35g protein (for the entire pint, including toppings/mix-ins)

Peanut Butter World Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 130 recipes like this one!

- 1 Chocolate Protein Shake
- 20-25g @Lakanto Monk Fruit sweetener
- 10g cocoa powder
- 1g (¼ tsp) salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 2 @OREO Thins, cream removed (I used 3 in the video bc my sister wanted more 😒)
- 15g peanut butter chips + 2g coconut oil + a pinch of salt
1. Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine the peanut butter chips, coconut oil, and salt, and melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between). Then, hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into a beautiful peanut butter swirl!
301 cal 24g C, 11g F, 35g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting
5. Respin again if powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with Oreos and melted peanut butter chips
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle

